INSERT INTO `chat_messages` VALUES (1,1,'USER','What is a port scan?','2026-07-07 14:18:35'),(2,1,'ASSISTANT','Port scanning (MITRE T1046/T1595) is reconnaissance to discover open ports and running services before an attack. Mitigation: close unused ports, deploy IDS/IPS to detect scan patterns, and use network segmentation.\n\nRecommended mitigation: Add the source IP to the watchlist, ensure unused ports are closed, and monitor for follow-up exploitation attempts.','2026-07-07 14:18:36'),(3,2,'USER','What is ransomware?','2026-07-07 14:24:57'),(4,2,'ASSISTANT','Ransomware encrypts victim data and demands payment for the decryption key, often after lateral movement via SMB (MITRE T1486). Mitigation: offline/immutable backups, network segmentation, least-privilege access, and rapid isolation of infected hosts.\n\nRecommended mitigation: Immediately isolate the affected host, disable shared network drives, and restore from the last known-good backup.','2026-07-07 14:24:58'),(5,3,'USER','How do I mitigate SQL injection?','2026-07-07 14:52:17'),(6,3,'ASSISTANT','Recommended mitigation for Sql Injection: Block the source IP at the WAF, sanitize/parameterize the vulnerable query, and review database audit logs for data exfiltration.','2026-07-07 14:52:18'),(7,4,'USER','What is the current threat level?','2026-07-08 07:29:08'),(8,4,'ASSISTANT','I don\'t have a specific answer for that yet, but I can help explain any of the nine detected threat categories (malware, DDoS, SQL injection, XSS, brute force, port scan, phishing, ransomware, insider threat), CVEs, MITRE ATT&CK techniques, or general cybersecurity concepts. Could you rephrase your question or ask about one of those topics?','2026-07-08 07:29:08'),(9,5,'USER','What is ransomware?','2026-08-11 15:51:46'),(10,5,'ASSISTANT','Ransomware encrypts victim data and demands payment for the decryption key, often after lateral movement via SMB (MITRE T1486). Mitigation: offline/immutable backups, network segmentation, least-privilege access, and rapid isolation of infected hosts.\n\nRecommended mitigation: Immediately isolate the affected host, disable shared network drives, and restore from the last known-good backup.','2026-08-11 15:51:48'),(11,5,'USER','why does this threat occur','2026-08-11 15:51:58'),(12,5,'ASSISTANT','I don\'t have a specific answer for that yet, but I can help explain any of the nine detected threat categories (malware, DDoS, SQL injection, XSS, brute force, port scan, phishing, ransomware, insider threat), CVEs, MITRE ATT&CK techniques, or general cybersecurity concepts. Could you rephrase your question or ask about one of those topics?','2026-08-11 15:51:58'),(13,5,'USER','what are the different types of attack','2026-08-11 15:52:15'),(14,5,'ASSISTANT','I don\'t have a specific answer for that yet, but I can help explain any of the nine detected threat categories (malware, DDoS, SQL injection, XSS, brute force, port scan, phishing, ransomware, insider threat), CVEs, MITRE ATT&CK techniques, or general cybersecurity concepts. Could you rephrase your question or ask about one of those topics?','2026-08-11 15:52:15'),(15,6,'USER','what is a threat','2026-08-11 16:12:11'),(16,6,'ASSISTANT','In cybersecurity, a threat is a potential occurrence that could compromise the confidentiality, integrity, or availability of an asset, system, or data. It\'s a possible event that could cause harm, such as unauthorized access, data breaches, or disruption of services. Threats can be intentional (e.g., malware, hacking) or unintentional (e.g., human error, natural disasters). Examples of threats include:\n\n* Malicious actors (hackers, insiders)\n* Malware (viruses, ransomware)\n* Vulnerabilities (unpatched software)\n* Denial-of-Service (DoS) attacks\n* Social engineering (phishing, spear phishing)\n\nTo mitigate threats, it\'s essential to identify, assess, and prioritize them, and then implement controls and countermeasures to reduce the risk of occurrence or impact.','2026-08-11 16:12:13'),(17,7,'USER','What is ransomware?','2026-09-07 04:30:45'),(18,7,'ASSISTANT','The AI assistant service is currently unavailable. Please try again shortly, or consult the Threat Intelligence page for CVE and MITRE ATT&CK details.','2026-09-07 04:30:46'),(19,8,'USER','What is ransomware?','2026-09-07 05:51:46'),(20,8,'ASSISTANT','The AI assistant service is currently unavailable. Please try again shortly, or consult the Threat Intelligence page for CVE and MITRE ATT&CK details.','2026-09-07 05:51:46');
